# Stripe PUBLISHABLE key for the checkout's Payment Element (ADR-0012).
# The variable is STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY. Baked at BUILD time via a Vite define —
# changing it needs a rebuild + redeploy.
# It is not a secret (it is published to every buyer's browser), but it is
# deliberately not a wrangler `var`: the wrangler guard test forbids any vars
# key matching /SECRET|KEY|TOKEN|PASSWORD/i, and that guard is worth keeping.
#
# Leaving it UNSET is a supported state: /checkout renders review + totals and
# says "Card payment isn't set up on this store yet.", creating no order. A
# value that IS set but does not look like pk_test_… / pk_live_… fails the
# build on purpose — a typo'd key is otherwise indistinguishable from no key,
# and would silently degrade every buyer.
#
# STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_replace_me

# Extra plugin egress hosts (build time; rebuild + redeploy to change).
# OTTA_EXTRA_ALLOWED_HOSTS is a comma-separated list of public DNS hostnames added
# to the plugin's ctx.http allowlist (beside api.stripe.com). These FAIL THE
# BUILD: wildcards; schemes, ports, paths; IPv4/IPv6 literals; single-label
# names; localhost, local, internal, localdomain, home.arpa, lan and names under
# them; nip.io, sslip.io, xip.io and names under them; any Stripe host other
# than api.stripe.com (js.stripe.com is browser-only, ADR-0012).
# This is a build-time sanity check, NOT SSRF protection: runtime protection is
# EmDash's egress check on the resolved IP (the Worker runs without
# global_fetch_strictly_public). Listing a host means trusting its DNS. Keep
# every host off the site's own Cloudflare zone.
#
# OTTA_EXTRA_ALLOWED_HOSTS=api.example.com,hooks.example.org

# NO secrets in this file or anywhere in the repo. The Worker's
# EMDASH_ENCRYPTION_KEY is set with `wrangler secret put` (see README).
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT (`astro dev`) needs one too, or no payment key can be saved
# in Settings (ADR-0037). Put a dev-only key in your copy of this file (`.env`
# is gitignored), generated with `npx emdash secrets generate`. Exporting it in
# the shell does not reach the dev Worker.
#
# EMDASH_ENCRYPTION_KEY=emdash_enc_v1_replace_me
